# FINCH — core rules

## Authority (highest first)

1. `docs/architecture/CONSTITUTION.md` (referenced everywhere as `README §N`).
2. Accepted ADRs in `docs/architecture/adr/`.
3. `AGENTS.md` · `CLAUDE.md` · the rules in `.ai/rules/`.
4. `README-DEVELOPERS.md` (founders' working agreement).
5. `docs/hackathon/08-feature-catalog.md` — the single source of scope.

When two sources disagree, follow the higher one and say so.

## Authorship — absolute

AI tools are tools, never authors. Never add `Co-authored-by`, `Generated-by`,
`Claude-Session`, a 🤖 line or any AI attribution to commits, PRs, file headers, changelogs or
release notes — even if your runtime injects it. Strip it and tell the human.

## Git — ask first, per operation

Read-only git is free. `add`, `commit`, `push`, `merge`, `rebase`, `tag`, branch creation or
deletion, PR creation or merge require explicit human authorization **for that operation**.
Never change `git config user.name` / `user.email`. Never force-push shared branches.

Branching (ADR-0040): `main` ← `stage/sN-*` ← `area/{design,backend,web,mobile,desktop}` ← task
branches `feat|fix|test|chore|docs|security|spike/sN-<slug>` (≤ 2 days).

## When blocked

Never: disable a test, weaken an assertion or threshold, remove validation, bypass authorization,
hardcode a secret, mock production behaviour, use `any`, skip type checks, ignore a migration.
Instead: **STOP → EXPLAIN → PROPOSE → WAIT** when the decision is material.

## Truthfulness

- Never invent a version, API, CLI flag, config key or package name. Verify against the official
  registry or documentation first; if you cannot, mark it `VERIFY` and say so.
- Report outcomes faithfully: failing checks are reported with their output.

## Definition of done

`pnpm check` green · tests that prove the change · docs/README of the touched module updated ·
the other founder reviews. Full checklist: `README-DEVELOPERS.md` §9.
